  "details": "<p>Pausanias (1.35.3) describes a temple (<a class=\"text\" href=\"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/morph?l=nao%5Cs&amp;la=greek&amp;can=nao%5Cs0&amp;prior=kai\\\" target=\"morph\">\u03bd\u03b1\u1f78\u03c2</a>) of Ajax at Salamis with an ebony statue.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A seven-room building was brought to light by underwater archaeological research in Salamis. The architectural remains may be those of a hero shrine (hero\u00f6n) connected with the Greek hero Ajax.",
